<title>USA: Hecla says it won Phoenix suit.</title>
<headline>Hecla says it won Phoenix suit.</headline>
<dateline>COEUR D'ALENE, Idaho 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hecla Mining Co said the Idaho State Supreme Court ruled in its favor in the Star Phoenix Mining Co lawsuit challenging Hecla's right to terminate Star Phoenix's lease of the Star-Morning mine in North Idaho in 1990.</p>
<p>The court today reversed the judgment against Hecla made in 1994 in Idaho district court.</p>
<p>The Supreme Court ruled Hecla acted properly, according to the terms of the lease agreement. The ruling releases $10 million in cash being held in escrow pending completion of the case. The court also awarded Hecla costs and attorney's fees.</p>
</text>
